title the mark law gets a door, and a meter stops quoting itself
prompt the baton -- take the booked lap; docs-geode carries the mark law
think Lap N was 3969, so N mod 5 read row 4, the Earth row, whose Cardinal seat is the very foundation the card booked for this lane. The rota and the booking agreed without being made to.
think The card books a weave, so the first question is where docs-geode already teaches naming. One page did -- demos, whose first demo runs dated_path_resolve and explains why the day repeats inside a folded filename. That page teaches the CLOCK half and had never taught the MARK half, and the study room, which teaches a newcomer how to read this tree, taught neither. Names are the first thing a reader meets in every room, before any prose. So the crux was that docs-geode taught how to check a claim and how to read a mistake, and never how to read a name.
think The weave, then, is three things rather than a link. study/README.md takes a third habit, read the name, ahead of the two it had, because you meet names before you meet claims. demos/README.md takes a fifth demo running announced_length_scan.sh, since the shelf's own bar is that every command was run before it was written down and the mark half deserved the runnable proof the clock half already had. wiki/README.md records both edges, because its own law says a page absent from its table is one the shelf has yet to admit.
think Touching demos meant honoring its own promise that the output is what it printed. Two of the four elder outputs had gone false in thirteen days, and the QA card could not see it -- truth_counted reads whether CITED PATHS resolve, and a stale quoted output cites nothing. That is %430 and %435's shape again, a Truth measuring the wrong surface, met a third time.
think Then the demo I wrote fed the meter it quotes. announcements_checked went 6 to 11, three of them attributed to the demos page for ladders it had merely reprinted. The scan's own comments already document three fixes of exactly this family -- a ledger row, a self-voting announcement, an ellipsis range -- and state the principle: a page must state the true reach beside the announcement to earn its pass. The meter's own output line does exactly that, so the repair was that same rule in a third syntax rather than a new one, and syntax-independent on purpose: skipping fenced blocks would also excuse a bare announcement sitting inside one.
think Checking the new foundation's inbound links found the wider gap. It sits on the council rota that every ship deep-reads, and foundations/README.md had no row for it -- nor for six more of the twelve rota documents that live in that room. A newcomer routed there by the study page could not find half of what the fleet reads daily.
obs The strongest evidence this lap produced was accidental. study/README.md fell B+/89 to B+/87 by GETTING LONGER -- the addition carried it past the eight-sentence floor, so a Register that had been freed to a silent 100 became an honestly scored 82 at 18 percent negative, under Door's ceiling. The page improved and its number fell, because the number had been free. That is exactly what the card's OPEN %430 argues, produced without trying.
obs The instrument fault was worse than a miscount, and only the control showed it. Against the unfixed scan the planted quotation reads forecasts_short=2 and verdict=living_forecast: the quoting page is BLAMED for a forecast it reprinted. So the roster goes red the day any quoted ladder falls short, rather than merely counting high. A fix proven only in the passing direction would have missed that.
obs Both roster reds are surfaced rather than closed, and neither is mine to close. commit_message_guard is the card's %431 -- ten of eleven readings green, SEED_PUBLISHER_ARMS 0 alone, and the publisher is untracked at the root by design, so the repair is gate %1. agent_jail passes every functional check then meets bwrap: Failed to make / slave: Operation not permitted, which is this seat refusing a nested namespace rather than a defect in the tree.
obs Scope held at one keystone -- docs-geode teaches how to read a name -- expressed across the pages the shelf's own laws require, plus the rota subset of the foundations index. The remaining 26 unindexed pages are reported rather than swept, because each needs a written meaning clause and that is a round of prose, not a mechanical insert.
